    "title": "The task",
    "body": "A warehouse floor: **S** marks the two charging stations, **#** marks shelves. For every free cell, find the walking distance to the **nearest** station. Instead of one search per cell, start one BFS from both stations at once.",
    "code": "function distances(grid, stations) {\n  const dist = grid.map((row) => row.map(() => undefined));\n  const queue = stations.map(([r, c]) => [r, c, 0]); // every source first\n  for (const [r, c] of stations) dist[r][c] = 0;\n  for (const [r, c, d] of queue) {\n    for (const [nr, nc] of neighbours(r, c)) {\n      if (free(nr, nc) && dist[nr][nc] === undefined) {\n        dist[nr][nc] = d + 1;\n        queue.push([nr, nc, d + 1]);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return dist;\n}",
